## 1. Research Question

> **Is the rise of generative AI reshaping the demand structure of data analyst positions in China’s first-tier cities—Beijing, Shanghai, Guangzhou, and Shenzhen—in terms of required skills, job responsibilities, and compensation?**

Does the rise of generative AI reshape the demand structure of data analyst positions—in terms of required skills, job responsibilities, and compensation—in China’s four first-tier cities: Beijing, Shanghai, Guangzhou, and Shenzhen?

## 2. Dataset Description

| Item            | Description                                                                                                                 |
| --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Data source     | Public job postings from 51job, available at [https://we.51job.com](https://we.51job.com)                                   |
| Search criteria | Job function category = “Data Analysis” (function code `7501`); work locations = Beijing, Shanghai, Guangzhou, and Shenzhen |
| Dataset size    | **805** valid job postings and **8** variables                                                                              |
| Collection date | 2026-05-12                                                                                                                  |
| File            | `data/51job_cleaned.csv` (CSV file encoded in UTF-8 with BOM)                                                               |

The dataset contains each job posting’s title, detail-page URL, salary information, recruiting company name, company ownership type, company size, scraping timestamp, and, most importantly, the **full job description text** including job responsibilities and qualification requirements. The full job description text will serve as the core corpus for subsequent NLP analysis, including the extraction of skill terms, AI-related keywords, and descriptions of job functions.

For detailed variable descriptions, please refer to [`docs/data_description.md`](docs/data_description.md).

